			<item>
				<title>The True Value of R&amp;D</title>
				<link>https://kin-design.is-cool.dev/posts/the-value-of-rnd/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:44:17 +0200</pubDate>
				<guid>https://kin-design.is-cool.dev/posts/the-value-of-rnd/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Image by &lt;a href=&#34;https://pixabay.com/users/hermann-130146/?utm**source=link-attribution&amp;amp;utm**medium=referral&amp;amp;utm**campaign=image&amp;amp;utm**content=462579&#34;&gt;Hermann Traub&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&#34;https://pixabay.com//?utm**source=link-attribution&amp;amp;utm**medium=referral&amp;amp;utm**campaign=image&amp;amp;utm**content=462579&#34;&gt;Pixabay&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Research and Development AKA R&amp;amp;D is a common branch in many big companies dedicated to &lt;strong&gt;“playing around”&lt;/strong&gt; with ideas until they strike something good.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation is not treated as an afterthought, but as a necessity for the survival of the company.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Companies have a metric called &lt;strong&gt;“R &amp;amp;D Intensity”&lt;/strong&gt;, the ratio of revenue spent on R&amp;amp;D. The riskier, or “growth oriented” the company is, the bigger the R&amp;amp;D intensity. Biotech is naturally a leader in the field.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>This is Koz!</title>
				<link>https://kin-design.is-cool.dev/posts/koz_intro/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:53:38 +0200</pubDate>
				<guid>https://kin-design.is-cool.dev/posts/koz_intro/</guid>
				<description>&lt;div class=&#34;player&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;button id=&#34;playButton&#34; type=&#34;button&#34; onclick=&#34;showContent(this)&#34;&gt;&#xA;    Play Koz in the browser!&#xA;  &lt;/button&gt;&#xA;  &lt;button id=&#34;stopButton&#34; type=&#34;button&#34; style=&#34;visibility: hidden;&#34; onclick=&#34;clearContent(this)&#34;&gt;&#xA;    Stop Koz.&#xA;  &lt;/button&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;button type=&#34;button&#34; onclick=&#34;openLink(&amp;#34;https://sasvel.itch.io/koz/rate&amp;#34;)&#34;&gt;Rate &amp;amp; Review&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;script&gt;&#xA;  function openLink(url) {&#xA;    window.open(url, &#34;_blank&#34;);&#xA;  }&#xA;&#xA;  function showContent(button) {&#xA;    const player = button.closest(&#34;.player&#34;);&#xA;    const stopButton = document.getElementById(&#34;stopButton&#34;)&#xA;    button.style.visibility = &#34;hidden&#34;;&#xA;    stopButton.style.visibility = &#34;visible&#34;;&#xA;&#xA;    const iframe = document.createElement(&#34;iframe&#34;);&#xA;    iframe.className = &#34;embed-container&#34;;&#xA;    iframe.src = &#34;https://itch.io/embed-upload/18108046?color=9e2835&#34;;&#xA;    iframe.frameBorder = &#34;0&#34;;&#xA;    iframe.allowFullscreen = true;&#xA;    player.appendChild(iframe);&#xA;  }&#xA;&#xA;  function clearContent(button) {&#xA;    const player = button.closest(&#34;.player&#34;);&#xA;    const playButton = document.getElementById(&#34;playButton&#34;)&#xA;&#xA;    player.querySelector(&#34;.embed-container&#34;)?.remove();&#xA;    playButton.style.visibility = &#34;visible&#34;;&#xA;    button.style.visibility = &#34;hidden&#34;;&#xA;  }&#xA;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;the-weird-yet-charming-idea&#34;&gt;The weird, yet charming idea.&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Koz started as an ambitious university project for a pygame course.&#xA;It was my first experience building a game outside of an engine and it was a wild one.&#xA;I wanted to make something like a visual representation of what is going on in my head when playing Scoundrel and go off from there.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
